      "writtenOn": "2026-01-16T03:26:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you intend repeat++ here? instead of repeat--?\n\nI\u0027m just worried once repeat is set, if the vendorhook doesn\u0027t modify it this would loop indefinitely. It seems less error prone for the vendorhook to set to a value that it will repeat at most that many times unless the vendorhook sets it again.",
      "revId": "196523d518f53df1f9d95e58dc1f183cb94e6cf2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ecfff0d1_02b8b329",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/ext.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4715,
      "author": {
        "id": 4363940
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-16T04:02:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you very much for your review:\nYes, we are using `repeat++` here for the following reasons:\n1. When entering for the first time, `repeat` is 0, so `vh` will increment it, indicating the first round.\n2. When ending this round, `ext` will set `repeat`, indicating the second round upon entry. If we find that the current round number matches our current round number, we will set it to -1. The loop will not restart after the current round is completed.\nWe are not using `repeat--` here because:\nIf we set the maximum round number upon entry, the `repeat` value would be 0 in both the first and last rounds. We would then need to use other variables to distinguish between the first and last entry values.",
      "parentUuid": "cc9d3d73_c10babb9",
      "revId": "196523d518f53df1f9d95e58dc1f183cb94e6cf2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
